# Line endings are decided here, once, rather than by whichever tool last
# wrote a file.
#
# This exists because it already went wrong. A scripted edit rewrote four
# source files from LF to CRLF, and because git had no opinion, the whole of
# each file landed in a commit as changed -- 4,842 lines of churn across
# mob.js, skill.js, mob.css and strings.css for edits that touched a handful.
# A diff that large is not reviewable, so a real mistake inside one would have
# gone through unseen. That is the cost being avoided: not tidiness, but the
# ability to read a change before it ships.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text; `eol=lf` normalises those in the
# repository. Working copies on Windows still check out however core.autocrlf
# says, so nothing about editing here changes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and must never be touched: WZ archives, sprites, audio, icons and
# the test fixtures. A newline "fix" inside any of these corrupts it silently,
# which is the exact failure mode this project spends most of its guards on.
*.wz      binary
*.ms      binary
*.img     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.mp3     binary
*.wav     binary
*.dll     binary
*.exe     binary
*.pdb     binary
*.zip     binary
*.snk     binary
